=== email subject
[End of life on 30 Nov 2026] Atlassian Confluence 7.19: security updates stop
=== email body
What's affected:
  Atlassian Confluence (Server and Data Center, the wiki the whole school has run on since before anyone can remember), version 7.2.8 (your note: head office firewall)
  That is release 7.19 on endoflife.date.

Why it matters:
  Security updates for Atlassian Confluence 7.19 stop on 30 Nov 2026, in 58 days. After that, newly found flaws in it, including ones attackers use, will not be fixed.

What to do before 30 Nov 2026:
  1. Upgrade to a supported release. The newest supported release listed on endoflife.date is 8.0 (latest version 8.0.1).
  2. Until you can upgrade, limit who can reach it (for example, no access from the internet) and keep an eye on its vendor's advisories.

Links:
  endoflife.date: https://endoflife.date/fortios
  Vendor lifecycle: https://www.fortinet.com/support/product-life-cycle

--
When you have dealt with it, run: patchtacio ack eol/fortinet-fortios/7.2
Patchtacio then stops reminding you about it.
You get this alert because Atlassian Confluence (Server and Data Center, the wiki the whole school has run on since before anyone can remember) is on your Patchtacio product list.
